notes
  * "dirty tracked files": the run used the zero-moment guard before it was
    committed; it is the commit that adds this file. The scripts/lib.py
    sha256 above pins the exact content (check: sha256sum scripts/lib.py).
  * An earlier run of this script (same day, before the guard) stopped at
    plotRuptureDynamics: scripts/lib.py magnitude = log10(moment) raised for
    fault 2 (zero slip at 20 steps), so no fault.dyna.r.nc was written.
  * Stand-ins as listed in roundtrip.py's docstring (zero EQquasi steps,
    synthetic infile1). Columns vxm..vzs and state_variable are 0 at 20 steps
    for this case; the nonzero column counts how many checked values are not 0.
